      "side": 1,
      "message": "General the change is LGTM. +2 assume the other comment is adjusted. Left a note to other reviewer here. But it shouldn\u0027t be a blocker for merge this change.\n\n\nTo other reviewers:\n\nI think this CL seems to be safe due to the following analysis:\n\nConntrackMonitoring:\n\nBefore and after change: 1) started when IpServer.BaseServingState is entered.\n 2) stopped when IpServer.BaseServingState is exited.\n\n\nThe timming is not changed.\n\n\nschedulePollingStats/scheduleConntrackTimeoutUpdate\n\nBefore the change: 1) started when Tethering.TetherModeAliveState is entered 2) stopped when Tethering.TetherModeAliveState is existed.\n\nAfter change: 1) started when IpServer.BaseServingState is entered.\n 2) stopped when IpServer.BaseServingState is exited.\n\n\n Once IpServer enter the TetheredState/LocalHotspotState, it will call `sendInterfaceState(mDesiredInterfaceState)`, then after one handler loop, Tethering.InitialState will change to Tethering.TetherModeAliveState.\n\n So after the change the schedulePollingStats/scheduleConntrackTimeoutUpdate is started a little bit early than before. But it start right after IpServer enter the TetheredState/LocalHotspotState so IpServer shouldn\u0027t miss any event.\n\n Same for stop, when TetheredState/LocalHotspotState, it will call `sendInterfaceState(mDesiredInterfaceState)`, hen after one handler loop, Tethering.TetherModeAliveState will transit to Tethering.InitialState. So aftaer the change, the schedulePollingStats/scheduleConntrackTimeoutUpdate is stopped a little bit early than  before. But as it only stop when all IpServer exit TetheredState/LocalHotspotState so it is safe.",
